<title>FRANCE: Usinor hopes for better earnings in 97.</title>
<headline>Usinor hopes for better earnings in 97.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Usinor Sacilor chairman Francis Mer said on Tuesday that he hoped the steelmaker would improve earnings in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;After not a very good first half 1997 linked to previous price declines, there should be a significant upturn in the second half of 1997 regarding earnings,&quot; he told a news conference. &quot;We are hoping to do better in 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>Earlier the steelmaker reported that 1996 profits fell to 1.49 billion francs from a record 4.43 billion francs the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
